## Operational notes and privacy

Read `LOCAL-NOTES.md` before ingesting or editing. The user's notes live there rather than in this shareable file. The config snapshot at `vault/.scaffold-config.json`, `raw/`, `vault/`, and evaluation cases are local by default and ignored by Git.

Apply exclusions and remove secrets **before** storing a Raw copy or sending material to a model. If a source may not be processed by this agent or model service, stop and use an authorized local path. This starter supplies instructions, not an automated privacy scanner or consent system. A model's access to a source does not authorize publishing it. Review every proposed export separately. Never push source-derived content to a remote by default.

---

## Read order

1. **`CLAUDE.md`** (this file) — schema, operational notes, conventions
2. **`vault/index.md`** — catalog of every page, grouped by category
3. **`vault/log.md`** — recent ingests, queries, lints, decisions (the last ~20 entries are usually enough)
4. **`vault/<category>/<page>.md`** — the actual content
5. **`raw/<source>`** — original source documents, checked when a source-dependent claim needs support

Stop once you have enough context. Reading the whole vault is rarely correct.

